[Task Description]
You are to evaluate the structure of the response to the user query. Focus exclusively on assessing organization, formatting, and sectional arrangement using the specified criteria.

[Criteria]
- Exceptionally Well-Structured (5 points): The response is impeccably organized with a clear hierarchy), logical sequencing, consistent formatting, and smooth transitions; structure notably enhances readability.
- Very Well-Structured (4 points): The response is clearly organized with appropriate paragraphing, itemization, or headings; ideas are presented in an orderly sequence with only very minor issues.
- Mostly Well-Structured (3 points): The response is generally organized but has minor structural issues .
- Basically Structured (2 points): The response shows noticeable structural problems (e.g., rambling blocks, missing organization cues) but remains followable.
- Poorly Structured (1 point): The response is difficult to follow due to significant disorganization, misuse of sections/bullets, or inconsistent formatting, though some structure is present.
- Not Well-Structured (0 points): The response lacks discernible organization and is difficult to navigate.

